# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and never committed.

# The model that tags and reviews your solves. Restart coach-web after changing it.
# A name with a slash (vendor/model) goes through OpenRouter and needs
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY; any other name goes to Anthropic and needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# Only the key your model needs is read, so you only need to fill in that one.
#
# Free, through OpenRouter (the default): fast, but not scored by the evals yet.
COACH_MODEL=nex-agi/nex-n2.5-pro:free
# Paid, through Anthropic: the model every eval number in RESULTS.md was measured on.
COACH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys - for vendor/model names. Free models there
# may log your prompts, which here means your code; check the model's page. A free
# account gets 50 requests a day across all free models (1000 after $10 of credit).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# https://console.anthropic.com -> API keys - for Claude model names.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Without the key your model needs, a logged solve is still stored and scheduled,
# just untagged (`coach enrich` fills the tags in once the key is there) and
# unreviewed. Nothing else calls the API.

# Only needed for identity-linked Anthropic keys, which the API rejects unless the
# request names the workspace it acts in. Standard keys can leave this unset.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...
